response:
Implementing a text editor with multiple lists (often referred to as "multitext") in an Angular application involves several steps. Below is a basic guide on how you can achieve this:

### Step 1: Create the Basic Structure

First, set up your Angular project and create the necessary components.

```bash
ng new multiTextEditor
cd multiTextEditor
```

### Step 2: Define the Components

Create two main components: `MultilistComponent` for managing multiple text areas and `EditorComponent` for the actual text editing functionality.

#### MultilistComponent.ts

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-multilist',
  templateUrl: './multilist.component.html'
})
export class MultilistComponent {
  public texts = [];
  public selectedTextIndex = -1;

  addNewText() {
    if (this.texts.length === 0) {
      return;
    }
    this.selectedTextIndex++;
    const newText = { id: this.selectedTextIndex };
    this.texts.push(newText);
  }

  removeSelectedText() {
    if (!this.selectedTextIndex || this.selectedTextIndex >= this.texts.length) {
      return;
    }
    this.texts.splice(this.selectedTextIndex, 1);
    this.selectedTextIndex--;
  }
}
```

#### MultilistComponent.html

```html
<div>
  <button (click)="addNewText()">Add New Text</button>
  <button (click)="removeSelectedText()" *ngIf="selectedTextIndex !== -1">Remove Selected Text</button>

  <div *ngFor="let text of texts; let i = index">
    <input type="text" [value]="text.id" />
  </div>
</div>
```

### Step 3: Implement Editor Component

Next, create the `EditorComponent` where users will input their text.

#### EditorComponent.ts

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { FormControl } from '@angular/forms';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-editor',
  template: `
    <textarea #editor></textarea>
    <button (click)="saveText(editor.value)">Save Text</button>
  `,
  styles: []
})
export class EditorComponent {
  private _control = new FormControl('');

  get control(): string {
    return this._control.value;
  }

  saveText(text: string): void {
    console.log('Saving text:', text);
  }
}
```

#### EditorComponent.html

```html
<textarea [(ngModel)]="control"></textarea>
<button>Save Text</button>
```

### Step 4: Connect the Components

Finally, connect the `MultilistComponent` and `EditorComponent`.

#### AppModule.ts

Ensure both components are included in your module:

```typescript
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { BrowserModule } from '@angular/platform-browser';
import { AppComponent } from './app.component';
import { MultilistComponent } from './multilist/multilist.component';
import { EditorComponent } from './editor/editor.component';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [
    AppComponent,
    MultilistComponent,
    EditorComponent
  ],
  imports: [
    BrowserModule
  ],
  providers: [],
  bootstrap: [AppComponent]
})
export class AppModule { }
```

### Step 5: Run Your Application

Run your Angular application using the following command:

```bash
ng serve
```

Open your browser and navigate to `http://localhost:4200` to see your text editor with multiple lists working together.

